{# Landmark (from a real drift): an earlier spec had 6 async endpoints, a job
   queue and a warning-acknowledgement flow — too heavy for v1. #}
Spec API: {{ ref('2_a_spec').api | tojson }}
Spec feature names: {{ ref('2_a_spec').features | map(attribute='name') | list | tojson }}

First, count the endpoints. An endpoint that takes an upload and returns the file
or JSON in the same response is synchronous and fine, whatever its name. Only an
endpoint that returns a job/build id to poll later, or a separate status/result
endpoint, counts as a queue or lifecycle. Then check whether any feature name is
about doing research (a feature that merely uses research findings does not count).
Fail only if: more than 3 endpoints, OR a queue/polling/lifecycle endpoint as
defined above, OR a research feature. Otherwise pass.

Reply with only JSON: {"results": "pass"} or {"results": "fail"}.
